# Build outputs.
#
# These are anchored to the repository root on purpose. Unanchored, `build-*/`
# matches ANY directory at ANY depth, which silently swallowed the whole
# `build-retarget` skill and its evaluation fixtures. A missing negative fixture
# does not fail the eval harness loudly - it just quietly weakens the gate - so
# these patterns must never be allowed to reach the skill or fixture trees.
# Build output from apps under test lives in `work/`, which is ignored entirely.
/build/
/build-*/
/out/
/dist/
/bin/
/obj/
*.user

# Application clones under test - these are separate git repos with their own
# history and must not be vendored into the workbench.
work/

# Port evidence: keep the shared state + directory structure, ignore bulky
# captures (screenshots, logs, perf traces, binaries) unless deliberately added.
artifacts/**
!artifacts/
!artifacts/PORT_STATE.json
!artifacts/**/
!artifacts/**/*.md

# Secrets — never commit these
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
id_rsa*
*.env
.env*
scripts/vm.env
scripts/vm.env.bak
!scripts/vm.env.example

# Credential dumps — az-cred.txt and anything that looks like one
az-cred*
*cred*.txt
*credential*
*secret*
*password*
*.credentials

# Windows / WSL cruft
*:Zone.Identifier
*:sec.endpointdlp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Node dependencies (contracts/evals)
node_modules/
